From 5aafcc61c1086a3cd29a1053a71c3149edb8ec21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frank Chang <frank.aka.hao.hao@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:47:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: add ASUS Tinker Edge R (RK3399Pro)

Port of ASUS's Linux 4.4 rk3399pro-tinker_edge_r.dts to this 6.1 vendor
tree, using the Toybrick RK3399ProD and rk3399pro-evb-v11-linux files as
templates for the 6.1 bindings.

 - RK809 PMIC on I2C0 with the Tinker Edge R rail voltages, FAN53555 for
   VDD_CPU_B (I2C0) and VDD_GPU (I2C8), eMMC (mmc-pwrseq-emmc reset),
   microSD with UHS modes and the 10 mA pad drive ASUS uses.
 - Type-C: FUSB302 as a TCPM port (fcs,fusb302) with a usb-c-connector,
   usb-role-switch to usbdrd_dwc3_0 (dual role) and the orientation switch
   to tcphy0, VBUS source via a fixed regulator on GPIO4_D1.
 - NPU over USB: usbdrd3_1 host, EHCI/OHCI hosts, npu_ref_clk pinmux,
   rk808-clkout2; nothing else is needed on the AP side (the firmware is
   loaded from userspace with npu_powerctrl/upgrade_tool).
 - PCIe x1 to the M.2 Key-E slot (RTL8822CE) with WL_REG_ON as
   vpcie3v3-supply, Bluetooth enable on GPIO2_D4.
 - HDMI (phy table), analogue audio (RK809 codec, headset detect), HDMI
   audio, RGMII gigabit (RTL8211F, external 125 MHz clock), LEDs, ADC keys,
   IMU/compass/EEPROM on I2C1, header I2C6/I2C7 enabled.
 - Camera path: vendor rkisp1 on both ISPs; a Toshiba TC358743 HDMI-RX
   bridge (Geekworm X1301) on CSI0/I2C1 by default, with a second DTB
   variant (-hdmirx-csi1) that puts it on CSI1/I2C2 instead.
 - Console: fiq debugger on UART0 (40-pin header pins 8/10, 115200).
 - cdn_dp (DisplayPort over Type-C) stays disabled like the Toybrick port.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
